@* Stylesheets="Manual": the app writes the theme's <link> tags into its own head, so the browser
   fetches the cockpit's fonts and rules with the first wave of the page instead of after .NET has
   started. The provider still verifies them and adds any that are missing.

   RespectSystemColorScheme is left at its default (true) on purpose: the app's default mode is "auto",
   and this provider is the only thing that reads prefers-color-scheme and hands it to the theme
   service. With it off, "auto" would have nothing to resolve against. Leaving it on also keeps the
   mode live - the interface follows the system while it is open, not only at startup. *@
<FlareThemeProvider Stylesheets="ThemeStylesheets.Manual">
    <Router AppAssembly="@typeof(App).Assembly">
        <Found Context="routeData">
            <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="@typeof(MainLayout)" />
            <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="routeData" Selector="h1" />
        </Found>
    </Router>
</FlareThemeProvider>
